WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.280 --> 00:00:09.520
Clinical trials help scientists better understand&nbsp;
health and disease better. By volunteering&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:14.240
for a clinical trial you may be helping your&nbsp;
community, our society, and people in general.&nbsp;

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:18.400
Joining a clinical trial may not help&nbsp;
you, but it could help your grandmother,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:22.800
your child, your neighbor, your friend,&nbsp;
or maybe even someone you’ve never met.

00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:28.000
It is possible that, during a clinical&nbsp;
trial, you may receive treatment&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:31.360
that helps you. While It is also&nbsp;
possible that the treatment or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:35.200
activity you do during a clinical&nbsp;
trial may not benefit you at all.

00:00:35.200 --> 00:00:39.680
Before you volunteer for a clinical trial,&nbsp;
find out all risks and benefits associated with&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:39.680 --> 00:00:45.040
participating in the trial so that you have all&nbsp;
the facts before making a decision. Ask questions.&nbsp;

00:00:45.680 --> 00:00:49.040
What is being studied?
What is the purpose of the clinical trial?&nbsp;

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:53.200
How long will the trial last?
How many study visits will I have to attend?&nbsp;

00:00:53.200 --> 00:00:55.680
What kinds of tests or&nbsp;
procedures will be preformed?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:56.720 --> 00:00:59.920
Blood tests or physical&nbsp;
examinations are just an example.&nbsp;

00:00:59.920 --> 00:01:03.440
Will I be able to take my regular&nbsp;
medicines during the clinical trial?&nbsp;

00:01:03.440 --> 00:01:09.680
What are the possible risks and benefits&nbsp;
of participating in the clinical trial? And&nbsp;

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:12.640
How will the results of the&nbsp;
clinical trial be shared with me?

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:16.000
When you have as much information&nbsp;
as possible about a clinical trial,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:19.120
you’ll feel much more confident&nbsp;
about the decision you make.

00:01:19.120 --> 00:01:22.640
Before you sign up for a clinical trial,&nbsp;
ask the people who are conducting the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:22.640 --> 00:01:26.880
trial to answer all of your questions. And&nbsp;
remember that you may stop participating&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:39.840
in the clinical trial at any time,&nbsp;
even after the study has started.

